        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-ud-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 6 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Fuel seasons by billing month. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in. The JSON-LD gates the fuel PriceDefinitions on calendar months, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month takes the other season's fuel price. (2) Franchise fee location. UD-18 serves single phase at 120V and 240V, which FCR-27 classes as Secondary Distribution, so its Secondary Distribution rates are the fuel prices, and the ProfileAlternatives set's voltage dimension has that one value, crossed with MFF-11's two locations in two alternatives. A consumer selects one, for example inside city limits. (3) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the non-energy charges' Prices, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (4) Estimated energy. The monthly energy and demand of an unmetered device are estimated by the Company and charged at the sheet's rate. The estimate is not carried; the prices apply to whatever kWh a consumer supplies. (5) Minimum Bill. The sheet sets it at the $18.00 Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, DSM, Fuel Cost Recovery on the current month's kWh and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every price here is zero or positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (6) Additional facilities and Term of Contract. Where facilities must be installed to serve the customer, the customer may be required to pay for them and their perpetual maintenance; the term is one year. Neither is priced on the sheet and neither is carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
